WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.534
-It seems like we planned this,

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.634
but this has been scheduled
for a long time.

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.033
No one could have imagined,
a couple of months ago,

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.334
what happened today.

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:10.434
How does this feel?

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:12.734
How are you processing it
as a New Yorker?

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:16.667
-Yeah, well, I mean, there's as
an American and as a New Yorker.

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:21.934
As a New Yorker, it was a very
New York kind of day.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:24.300
You have not just
what was happening

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.000
with former president Trump,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.100
but then you have
MTG flying into town.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.801
You've got, you know, just
the whole chaos of the scene

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:35.000
and also all the people
walking by like,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.601
"Okay, I'm on my lunch break.

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:39.067
Time to go."
-Yeah.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.734
-You know, it was --
it was just a lot.

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:43.033
It was a circus, right?

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.067
-I mean, your whole life,
this is a person who,

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:48.934
especially in New York,
has been investigated,

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:52.467
never charged,
you know, multiple,

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:56.033
you know, certainly accusations
of financial improprieties.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.400
Did you ever think
this day would come

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.834
where he would be arraigned,

00:00:58.834 --> 00:01:02.567
especially for things like,
you know, the misuse of money?

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:06.300
-Yeah, I mean,
I think I had always felt

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.634
that something might happen.

00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:11.501
Honestly,
I think if something did,

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.601
I would have thought
it would be something like this,

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:17.934
around falsification of business
documents or some sort of charge

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:20.434
that has to do
with documentation or finances.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:22.868
But, I mean,
my dad was an architect.

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:26.367
He worked in construction
and in that industry.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:27.968
And from the time
I was a kid,

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:31.801
it's like no one knew this guy
better than New Yorkers.

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:36.367
And just like this is just --
People would have thought

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:38.534
this is what he would have been
in for before he was president.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.000
-Yeah.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.067
-So, you know, I think it does
feel like a matter of course.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:46.267
I also think that --
I mean, listen,

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:49.801
this is not about guaranteeing
one outcome or another.

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:55.234
This is about due process,
and the lack of process of,

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:58.267
I think, a formal due process
for so long

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:00.200
really created
this question of,

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.467
"Do we really have
an equal society,

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:05.834
no matter your income,
no matter how powerful you are?"

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:09.400
And I think the presence
of this process demonstrates

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.400
that we should have one law
that applies to all people,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.634
no matter who you are
or where you come from.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

